window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-44471eb3eae1b363"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"fix-and-verify-security-findings\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">修复并验证安全发现项</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>从一条你认可其证据的发现项开始。生成补丁、审阅补丁，并针对更改后的代码验证原始问题。生成或应用补丁本身并不代表修复已经验证。</p> <p>在桌面工作台中，生成补丁不会更改当前选中的代码工作副本（checkout，可理解为当前打开并用于处理代码的副本）。应用补丁会更改该代码工作副本。验证过程会检查补丁并记录证据，但不会自动关闭发现项。</p> <p><a id=\"fix-a-finding-in-the-ui\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">在界面中修复发现项</h2> <p>从 <strong>Findings（发现项）</strong>或 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>中的已完成扫描打开一条已认可的发现项。审阅证据，然后使用 <strong>Patch（补丁）</strong>生成、审阅、应用并验证修复。</p> <ol> <li>生成补丁</li> </ol> <p>打开发现项，选择 <strong>Patch（补丁）</strong>标签页，然后选择 <strong>Generate patch（生成补丁）</strong>。在可行时，Codex 会验证或复现问题，并生成补丁文件，但不会修改所选代码工作副本。</p> <ol> <li>审阅拟议的差异</li> </ol> <p>检查受影响的代码和测试。确认此次更改解决了该发现项，且没有夹带无关重构，也没有削弱安全控制。</p> <ol> <li>在本地应用补丁</li> </ol> <p>只有在差异可接受后，才选择 <strong>Apply patch（应用补丁）</strong>。Codex 会将生成的补丁原样应用到工作树，并记录该状态。继续之前，请审阅工作树差异。</p> <ol> <li>验证修复</li> </ol> <p>选择 <strong>Verify fix（验证修复）</strong>。Codex 会重新运行原始复现步骤或其他利用漏洞的检查。如果可以运行回归测试，它会检查修复前测试是否失败、修复后是否通过。否则，它会记录验证缺口和已完成的检查。它还会检查正常行为、附近可能存在的绕过方式和代码库测试。</p> <ol> <li>关闭发现项</li> </ol> <p>验证不会自动关闭发现项。请审阅命令、结果和仍未弥补的证据缺口，然后填写准确的原因关闭发现项，或将其保持为未解决状态以便继续处理。</p> <blockquote> <p>截图未离线保存: Codex Security 工作台显示一条已认可发现项的生成补丁</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> 将安全修复应用到代码工作副本之前，先审阅生成的补丁。 </figcaption> <p><a id=\"fix-a-finding-in-a-conversation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">在对话中修复发现项</h2> <p>使用已安装的插件处理扫描、工单、安全公告或其他审查中发现的问题。提供发现项 ID 和报告路径；如果有复现步骤或验证命令，也请一并提供：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:fix-finding to fix finding &lt;finding-id&gt; from &lt;report-path&gt;. Verify the issue against this checkout, fix it, and test the original failure and legitimate behavior. Record any verification you couldn't complete.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 $codex-security:fix-finding，修复 &lt;report-path&gt; 中的发现项 &lt;finding-id&gt;。结合当前检出的代码核实问题、完成修复，并测试原始失败情形和正常合法行为。记录任何未能完成的验证。</div></div> <p>这会授权修改当前代码工作副本。Codex 可以检查代码库以补充缺失的技术细节，但在选择修复方案前，可能需要你澄清预期的安全策略。</p> <p><a id=\"run-remediation-without-interaction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">无交互地运行修复流程</h2> <p>如需运行可重复的扫描和补丁生成，请使用独立 CLI 的<a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=codex-security-validate-and-codex-security-patch\">验证和补丁命令</a>。</p> <p>若要通过 Codex CLI 调用已安装的插件，请先在运行器的 <code>CODEX_HOME</code> 中安装 Codex Security。全新运行器默认不包含 Marketplace 插件。针对每条已认可的发现项，使用单独的代码工作副本或作业：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex exec --sandbox workspace-write 'Use $codex-security:fix-finding to fix finding &lt;finding-id&gt; from &lt;report-path&gt;. Verify the issue against this checkout, fix it, and test the original failure and legitimate behavior. Record any verification you could not complete.'\n</code></pre> <p>可写沙盒允许工作流编辑源代码和测试。请保留补丁及验证证据供审阅。有关安装、扫描设置和文件处理，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af?anchor=automate-reviews-in-cicd\">CI/CD 中的自动化审查</a>。</p> <p>验证通过后，按你们日常的代码审查流程合并更改。如果验证不完整，请将发现项保持为未解决状态，并注明剩余工作。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"fix-and-verify-security-findings\">Fix and verify security findings</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Start with one finding whose evidence you accept. Generate a patch, review it, and verify the original issue against the changed code. A generated or applied patch isn't yet a verified fix.</p> <p>In the desktop workbench, generation leaves the selected checkout unchanged. Applying the patch changes that checkout. Verification checks the patch and records evidence without automatically closing the finding.</p> <h2 id=\"fix-a-finding-in-the-ui\">Fix a finding in the UI</h2> <p>Open an accepted finding from <strong>Findings</strong> or a completed scan in <strong>Scans</strong>. Review its evidence, then use <strong>Patch</strong> to generate, review, apply, and verify a fix.</p> <ol> <li>Generate a patch</li> </ol> <p>Open the finding, select the <strong>Patch</strong> tab, and select <strong>Generate patch</strong>. Codex validates or reproduces the issue when feasible and writes a patch artifact without modifying the selected checkout.</p> <ol> <li>Review the proposed diff</li> </ol> <p>Check the affected code and tests. Confirm that the change addresses the finding without unrelated refactors or weakened security controls.</p> <ol> <li>Apply the patch locally</li> </ol> <p>Select <strong>Apply patch</strong> only after the diff is acceptable. Codex applies the exact generated patch to the working tree and records that state. Review the working-tree diff before continuing.</p> <ol> <li>Verify the fix</li> </ol> <p>Select <strong>Verify fix</strong>. Codex reruns the original reproducer or another exploit check. When it can run a regression test, it checks that the test fails before the fix and passes after it. Otherwise, it records the verification gap and the checks it could complete. It also checks legitimate behavior, nearby bypasses, and repository tests.</p> <ol> <li>Close the finding</li> </ol> <p>Verification doesn't automatically close a finding. Review the commands, results, and remaining proof gap, then close the finding with an accurate reason or keep it open for more work.</p> <blockquote> <p>Screenshot not stored offline: Native Codex Security workbench showing the generated patch for an accepted finding</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> Review the generated security fix before applying it to your checkout. </figcaption> <h2 id=\"fix-a-finding-in-a-conversation\">Fix a finding in a conversation</h2> <p>Use the installed plugin with a finding from a scan, ticket, advisory, or other review. Supply the finding ID and report path, plus a reproducer or validation command if you have one:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:fix-finding to fix finding &lt;finding-id&gt; from &lt;report-path&gt;. Verify the issue against this checkout, fix it, and test the original failure and legitimate behavior. Record any verification you couldn't complete.\n</code></pre> <p>This authorizes edits to the checkout. Codex can inspect the repository for missing technical details, but may need you to clarify an intended security policy before choosing a fix.</p> <h2 id=\"run-remediation-without-interaction\">Run remediation without interaction</h2> <p>For repeatable scans and patch generation, use the standalone CLI <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=codex-security-validate-and-codex-security-patch\">validate and patch commands</a>.</p> <p>To invoke the installed plugin through Codex CLI, install Codex Security in the runner's <code>CODEX_HOME</code> first. A fresh runner doesn't include marketplace plugins by default. Use a separate checkout or job for each accepted finding:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex exec --sandbox workspace-write 'Use $codex-security:fix-finding to fix finding &lt;finding-id&gt; from &lt;report-path&gt;. Verify the issue against this checkout, fix it, and test the original failure and legitimate behavior. Record any verification you could not complete.'\n</code></pre> <p>The writable sandbox allows the workflow to edit source and tests. Preserve the patch and verification evidence for review. For installation, scan setup, and artifact handling, see <a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af?anchor=automate-reviews-in-cicd\">Automate reviews in CI/CD</a>.</p> <p>After verification, merge the change through your normal code-review process. If verification is incomplete, keep the finding open with the remaining work.</p>"};
